  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Thursday...\n\nAs upper level ridging builds in through Saturday, conditions will\nremain warm and dry with above average temperatures in the 60s \nand 70s. Ahead of a dry cold front anticipated Saturday night,\na modest pressure gradient over the Absaroka-Bearthooths and\n30-40kts winds aloft will create windy conditions across the\nfoothills west of Billings (Nye, Livingston, Big Timber).\nStrongest winds are likely to occur Saturday morning into the \nearly afternoon with gusts 40-50 mph expected, with about a 20%\nchance for gusts to 60 mph. The cold front Saturday night is not \nexpected to bring much wind with it, just cooler temperatures for \nSunday with highs in the 55-65 degree range. Temperatures are \nexpected to increase back into the upper 60s/low 70s for Monday \nand Tuesday as heights build back in ahead of troughing over the \nwest coast. There is still uncertainty on the track of this low \nfor the latter half of the week, but moderate chances at southwest\nflow Tuesday is giving the higher terrain across south-central MT\nlow chances for precipitation. TS",
